# expects: with inline record annotation passes conservatively — builtin-check-type is only
# invoked when the annotation serializes to a plain type-name String (e.g., "String", "Int").
# Dict annotations (@[x: Int]) produce type "Dict" not "String" via builtin-type-of doc.expects,
# so the validation is skipped and evaluation proceeds normally.
--- expects: @[x: Int]
[x: "hello"]
=== out
Dict({"x": String("hello")})
